  "note": "Seeing the key's chords inside one natural minor scale position, then using them in a solo: a scale-neck with `chords` rings each triad in the position, a chord-steps riff strikes each triad and picks its notes, a solo-over lights each chord's triad as a `stab` to strike on beat 1 and leaves the rest of the bar free, and a last chord-steps cuts each triad to a double stop on the top two strings. The old Variant selectors (one per key) are now moves (any key, 70 to 90 bpm), so the text names the key only as {{=key}}, the chords are counted the long way once as chord tokens, and a {{?key}} line says what stays the same.",
