        "heading": "The chords in the position",
        "minutes": 3,
        "cells": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Below is the neck with the notes of the {{=key}} natural minor scale in one position, and a row of four of its chords. {{chord:i}} is the 1st chord of the key, built on {{1}}. {{chord:iv}} is the 4th chord, built on {{4}}, {{chord:bVI}} the 6th, built on {{b6}}, and {{chord:bVII}} the 7th, built on {{b7}}.\nPress a chord in the Chords row below to ring its notes in the position and hear it. Play that chord as a triad on the G, B and high e strings, then play the scale notes around it.\nPractice until your hand finds each chord without looking at the neck.\n{{?key}}In another key the position sits on other frets, and each chord keeps its place inside it."
          },
